---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import site from '../../site.config.json' with { type: 'json' };

const page = {
  url: '/editorial-policy/', title: 'Editorial and Sourcing Policy',
  seoTitle: 'Marine Diesel Editorial & Sourcing Policy', pageType: 'policy',
  status: 'ready', author: site.defaultAuthor, reviewer: null,
  needsReviewer: false, parent: '/', parentTitle: 'Home',
  schema: ['WebPage', 'BreadcrumbList'], updated: site.legalUpdated,
  indexable: true, blockers: [], faqs: [],
  headings: [
    { depth: 2, slug: 'source-hierarchy', text: 'Our source hierarchy' },
    { depth: 2, slug: 'technical-and-safety-claims', text: 'Technical and safety claims' },
    { depth: 2, slug: 'prices-and-business-listings', text: 'Prices and business listings' },
    { depth: 2, slug: 'publishing-tools-and-ai', text: 'Publishing tools and AI' },
    { depth: 2, slug: 'updates-and-corrections', text: 'Updates and corrections' },
  ],
  description: 'How Marine Diesel Engine Australia researches, sources, reviews, updates and corrects marine engine guides, price information and business listings.',
  primaryKeyword: 'marine diesel editorial policy', searchIntent: 'Informational',
};
---
<Page page={page}>
  <h1>Editorial and sourcing policy</h1>
  <p>
    This policy explains how Marine Diesel Engine Australia selects evidence,
    handles uncertainty and keeps commercial information separate from general
    guidance. It applies to articles, guides, business listings and structured
    data published on this site.
  </p>

  <h2 id="source-hierarchy">Our source hierarchy</h2>
  <p>
    For specifications, procedures and service intervals, the operator,
    workshop and installation manuals for the exact engine, gearbox or drive
    take priority. We then prefer Australian government and regulator material,
    recognised safety organisations, manufacturer technical bulletins and
    established standards. Secondary sources may help explain a concept but do
    not override a current primary source.
  </p>
  <p>
    Sources must be relevant to the claim. A general manufacturer page is not
    evidence for a model-specific torque value, and an overseas price is not an
    Australian market price without clearly stated conversion and assumptions.
  </p>

  <h2 id="technical-and-safety-claims">Technical and safety claims</h2>
  <p>
    Safety warnings are written conservatively. When a symptom can indicate
    fire, flooding, fuel spray, loss of lubrication, loss of cooling or internal
    damage, the guide directs the reader to stop and obtain qualified help.
    Exact fluids, clearances, torque values and replacement intervals should be
    checked against the serial-number-specific manual before work begins.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not describe content as technically reviewed unless a reviewer is
    identified. The organisational editorial byline is not a substitute for a
    named credential or an inspection of the reader's vessel.
  </p>

  <h2 id="prices-and-business-listings">Prices and business listings</h2>
  <p>
    A price range should state its geography, collection date, sample or source,
    inclusions and important assumptions. Until those conditions are met, we
    explain the variables that shape a quote instead of inventing a number.
    Business details are published only from an attributable record and may be
    removed or corrected on request. Inclusion is not an endorsement.
  </p>
  <p>
    Any paid referral or commercial relationship must be disclosed where it can
    influence a reader's choice. Editorial guidance is not sold as favourable
    coverage.
  </p>

  <h2 id="publishing-tools-and-ai">Publishing tools and AI</h2>
  <p>
    We may use software and AI-assisted tools for research organisation,
    drafting, editing, image preparation, internal linking and quality checks.
    These tools can make confident mistakes. Their output is treated as draft
    material and is not itself a source. Claims still require an appropriate
    primary or authoritative reference, and no tool can inspect a vessel.
  </p>

  <h2 id="updates-and-corrections">Updates and corrections</h2>
  <p>
    Pages carry a last-updated date when available. Material changes should be
    rechecked against current sources; outdated or incomplete directory pages
    may be withheld from search indexing until their core information is ready.
    Reports are handled under our <a href="/corrections/">corrections policy</a>.
    You can also <a href="/contact/">send evidence or feedback</a> directly.
  </p>
</Page>
